@startuml
title TriggerIQ ERP - Zero Trust Security Model

cloud "Identity Provider (IdP)\n(Keycloak / Auth0 / OIDC)" as IdP
cloud "Zero Trust Policy Engine" as ZTPolicy
cloud "Monitoring & SIEM\n(ELK / Splunk / Prometheus)" as SIEM

actor Customer
actor Supplier
actor FinanceDept

rectangle "ERP System" {
  [Sales Module]
  [Inventory Module]
  [Finance Module]
  [AI/ML Module]
}

database "ERP Database\n(Encrypted PostgreSQL)" as DB
collections "Blockchain Ledger\n(Immutable + Encrypted)" as BC

' --- User Access ---
Customer --> IdP : Authenticate
Supplier --> IdP : Authenticate
FinanceDept --> IdP : Authenticate

IdP --> Customer : Token (short-lived)
IdP --> Supplier : Token (short-lived)
IdP --> FinanceDept : Token (short-lived)

' --- Service-to-Service Access ---
[Sales Module] --> ZTPolicy : Verify token & role
[Inventory Module] --> ZTPolicy : Verify token & role
[Finance Module] --> ZTPolicy : Verify token & role
[AI/ML Module] --> ZTPolicy : Verify token & role

' --- Data Access ---
[Sales Module] --> DB : Encrypted query
[Finance Module] --> DB : Encrypted query
[Inventory Module] --> DB : Encrypted update
DB --> ZTPolicy : Check data access rules

' --- Blockchain Access ---
[Sales Module] --> BC : Record transaction
[Finance Module] --> BC : Record payment
[AI/ML Module] --> BC : Validate integrity
BC --> ZTPolicy : Verify smart contract policy

' --- Monitoring ---
[ERP System] --> SIEM : Logs, metrics, alerts
BC --> SIEM : Transaction logs
DB --> SIEM : Access logs
ZTPolicy --> SIEM : Policy decision logs

note bottom
Zero Trust Principles:
- Never trust, always verify
- Least privilege access
- Encrypt everything
- Continuous monitoring
end note

@enduml